UPDATE 2026-09-05 (seat03): ablated (fresh oracle vs SCRIP, first divergence only, not fully root-caused).
FIRST DIVERGENCE, and it looks larger than most of this row's other residual markers: the test's own
internal self-check (`test delete: N, K` followed by a `not generated: ...` report when the check fails)
PASSES cleanly under real icont/iconx (`test delete: 41, 3	[ok]`, no failure report) but FAILS under SCRIP
for the very first case, printing dozens of "not generated" values (e.g. `not generated: 36 39 40 41` for
the first case alone, growing to ~90 missing values on the second case at line 5). The program name
("gener") and the self-check's own wording ("not generated") both point at Icon GENERATOR semantics under
structure mutation (deleting elements from a structure while a generator is actively iterating it, or a
similar suspend/resume-across-mutation shape) -- this smells like a real, likely nontrivial generator-
correctness gap rather than a narrow formatting bug, but NOT localized further this session (no source
read, no bisection). Given the size of the divergence, this is a strong ablation-bisection candidate for
whoever picks it up next -- likely deserves the same procedure-by-procedure narrowing `sorting` and `misc`
already got, not a guess from the symptom alone.
UPDATE 2026-09-05 (seat06): ROOT-MECHANISM PINNED AND ROWED, not just ablated. Bisected the `tdel` (delete-
while-generating) half to a 14-line, argv-free minimal witness confirmed in both m3 and m4: SCRIP's `!s`
set generator, after yielding an element the loop body then deletes, fails to seek forward to whatever
else is still live in the set (icont's own generator always either continues correctly or correctly has
nothing left). Smallest failing case: a 3-element set, 2 deletions per generated item. Rowed as
`icon-set-generator-does-not-resume-past-a-deleted-current-element` (rank 2, hq_B), with the ablation
trail and a concrete next bisection step -- this row's own DONE-WHEN is that mint's, not a re-derivation.
The `tins` (insert-while-generating) half shows a DIFFERENT-shaped failure (both "not generated" AND real
"generated twice" duplicates) -- flagged in that row as a plausibly-related but NOT verified same-mechanism
sibling, deliberately not folded in (work in classes, one witness per class). This marker itself is not yet
resolved (curing src/ is hq_B's, not this walker's) -- it stays as a marker pointing at the new row.
